# NOTE: `.github/workflows/` was ignored here with the comment "requires OAuth
# scope we don't have". That is no longer true — the configured token carries
# the `workflow` scope — and the entry had become self-defeating: the repo
# documented a blocking QA suite and a 95% coverage gate while ignoring the
# one file that would let anyone verify either claim. CI now lives in
# .github/workflows/qa.yml and is tracked.

# Temporary/generated docs at the REPOSITORY ROOT (keep only final summaries).
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. A gitignore pattern without one matches at
# ANY depth, so these root-level scratch names were silently swallowing tracked
# plan documents: `CLAUDE/Plan/.../PHASE-1-MEASUREMENT.md` and
# `CLAUDE/Plan/Completed/00025-.../STATUS.md` were both ignored, never
# committed, and linked to from their own PLAN.md — so the links resolved for
# the author and for nobody else.
#
# That is the worst shape of failure this file can produce: `git status` stays
# clean, no check fires, and the loss is invisible until someone else follows
# the link. CLAUDE/Plan/ is tracked source by policy (see CLAUDE/Plan/CLAUDE.md),
# so nothing under it may be caught by a convenience pattern meant for the root.
/COVERAGE_REPORT.md
/PHASE-*.md
/STATUS.md
/WORK_COMPLETED.md
/verify-*.sh

# Development artifacts and QA outputs
untracked/

# Claude Code managed worktrees (path not configurable, must be gitignored)
.claude/worktrees/

# Scheduled-tasks runtime lock (ScheduleWakeup/cron mechanism)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Acceptance test results
CLAUDE/AcceptanceTests/results/*
!CLAUDE/AcceptanceTests/results/.gitkeep

# ClaudeMdInjector backup (written before each injection to enable recovery)
.CLAUDE.md.pre-inject

# Secret word lists for the sensitive_content handler — never tracked. A
# term in one of these files must never reach git history; this rule ships
# BEFORE any such file is created so a broad `git add` can never catch one.
*.secret
*.secrets
